---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /happy-hour/
pageKey: happyHour
title: "Tajima Happy Hour | San Diego"
description: "Happy hour at Tajima Ramen in San Diego. Which rooms run it, and how to check today's times. Plaza Bonita is quick-serve and does not serve alcohol."
---
{#
  /happy-hour/. Brief: SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md.

  This page earns 1,361 clicks with ZERO internal links pointing at it. It
  catches 1,107 happy-hour clicks across 165 queries; all six location pages
  combined catch 32, because "tajima happy hour" contains no location and a
  location page cannot answer it. It is now linked from the footer, /menu/,
  and the Convoy address plate.

  Per Steve, it stays OUT of the header nav tonight. Adding a fifth item to a
  header signed off with four is a design decision, not a build one.

  ============================ TIMES AND PRICES ARE PULLED ============================

  This page previously rendered per-location windows (11:30am to 6:00pm, and
  Convoy's late-night Fri/Sat) plus drink and food prices, all carried from the
  design concept. They were removed on Steve's call and the reasoning is the
  same one that keeps opening hours off every other page: CLIENT_FACTS.md
  forbids publishing hours the door does not honor, a happy hour window is the
  same promise, and the failure mode is someone driving over at 5 for a window
  that shut at 4. The prices were worse: CLAUDE.md says menu prices are never
  published without client approval and nobody at Tajima has seen these.

  The markup for windows, drinks, and food is still below, behind an `if`.
  Populate _data/happyHour.json with real values from Amanda and it renders
  again. Do not restore the concept values.

  WHAT SURVIVES IS ONLY WHAT TRACES TO CLIENT_FACTS.md:
    - happy hour exists and varies by room
    - Plaza Bonita is quick-serve with no alcohol, so it has none
    - East Village runs Padres game-night beer specials and longer hours on
      home game nights. EAST VILLAGE ONLY. Not widened to the other rooms, and
      the concept's "$3.50 every tap beer, all locations" is gone with the rest.
#}

<section class="hh-hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="hh-hero__inner">
    <span class="hh-hero__eyebrow">San Diego</span>
    <h1 class="hh-hero__title" id="page-title">Happy Hour</h1>
    <p class="hh-hero__sub">
      Happy hour runs at most of the San Diego rooms, and the window is not the same everywhere. We are confirming the current times room by room. Until they are up here, call the one you are heading to and they will tell you. <a href="/locations/">Find your Tajima</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<nav class="hh-jumps" aria-label="Jump to a location">
  {%- for hh in happyHour.locations %}
  <a class="hh-jumps__btn" href="#hh-{{ hh.id }}">{{ hh.name }}</a>
  {%- endfor %}
</nav>

<section class="hh-grid" aria-label="Happy hour by location">
  <div class="hh-grid__inner">
    {%- for hh in happyHour.locations %}
    {%- set loc = (locations.items | where("id", hh.id)) | first %}
    <article class="hh-card" id="hh-{{ hh.id }}">
      <h2 class="hh-card__name"><a href="{{ loc.url }}">{{ hh.name }}</a></h2>

      {%- if hh.noAlcohol %}
      {#
        Brief section 4: "Plaza Bonita: no alcohol. Say it plainly."
        This is confirmed, so it is stated outright rather than left as a gap
        for someone to drive to National City and discover.
      #}
      <p class="hh-card__no-alcohol">
        Plaza Bonita is quick-serve inside the mall and does not serve alcohol, so there is no happy hour here. The bowls are the same bowls.
      </p>

      {%- elif hh.windows | length %}
      {# Renders only when _data/happyHour.json holds confirmed values. #}
      <div class="hh-card__hours">
        {%- for window in hh.windows %}
        <div class="hh-card__hours-row">
          <span>{{ window.time }}</span>
          <span class="hh-card__hours-days">{{ window.days }}</span>
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>

      <div class="hh-card__lists">
        {%- if hh.drinks | length %}
        <div>
          <p class="hh-card__list-label">Drinks</p>
          <ul class="hh-card__list">
            {%- for item in hh.drinks %}
            <li><span>{{ item.name }}</span><span>{{ item.price }}</span></li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if hh.food | length %}
        <div>
          <p class="hh-card__list-label">Food</p>
          <ul class="hh-card__list">
            {%- for item in hh.food %}
            <li><span>{{ item.name }}</span><span>{{ item.price }}</span></li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>

      {%- else %}
      {#
        No confirmed times for this room. The card still does the useful half
        of its job: it names the room, routes to it, and hands over a phone
        number that IS confirmed. It does not hold space for a value we do not
        have, and it does not promise one is coming on a date nobody set.
      #}
      <p class="hh-card__pending">
        Times are being confirmed. Call the room and they will tell you what is running today.
      </p>
      <a class="hh-card__phone" href="tel:+1-{{ loc.phone | replace('(', '') | replace(') ', '-') | replace(' ', '-') }}">{{ loc.phone }}</a>
      {%- endif %}

      <span class="hh-card__tag">{{ hh.tag }}</span>
    </article>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

{# ==================== PADRES ==================== #}
{#
  Brief section 3, scoped down to what CLIENT_FACTS.md actually confirms.
  Its East Village entry: "Padres game-night beer specials and extended hours
  on home game nights." That is this room and no other. The concept's "every
  tap beer $3.50, all SD locations except Plaza Bonita" carried a price and a
  scope that appear nowhere in CLIENT_FACTS.md, and both are gone.

  Still date-bounded in reality. SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md's position is that
  time-bound promos belong on GBP Posts. One block, deletable as one block.
#}
<section class="hh-padres" aria-labelledby="padres-title">
  <div class="hh-padres__inner">
    <p class="hh-padres__text">
      <strong id="padres-title">{{ happyHour.padres.headline }}.</strong>
      {{ happyHour.padres.body }}
    </p>
    <a class="hh-padres__link" href="/tajima-east-village/">See East Village</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="loc-close" aria-labelledby="close-title">
  <div class="loc-close__inner">
    <h2 class="loc-close__title" id="close-title">Pick a room.</h2>
    <p class="loc-close__sub">
      Happy hour is per location and so is the menu. <a href="/menu/">See the menu</a>, or <a href="/locations/">see all six San Diego rooms</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
